  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I have expression for 12 patients with a rare autoimmune disease, already log-transformed and mean-centred per gene. I'd like a gene-gene co-expression network for each patient separately, with p-values for every edge saved alongside."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like a gene-gene co-expression network for each patient separately, with p-values for every edge saved alongside.\" -- available from BONOBO.\n\nSeveral registered methods fit this result; they differ in their modeling assumptions:\n\n- **LIONESS-COEXPRESSION** — LIONESS represents the cohort network through sample contributions: W_q = N*W_all - (N-1)*W_without_q, where N is the cohort size and the same base estimator is fitted with and without sample q. Needs expression matrix.\n- **BONOBO** — BONOBO applies Bayesian estimation and shrinkage to sample-specific gene-gene co-expression. Needs expression matrix.\n\nWhich result do you mean: inferred gene-to-gene associations, one result per sample (LIONESS-COEXPRESSION or BONOBO); or p-value matrix paired with a sample-specific gene-gene co-expression result (BONOBO)?\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
